        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "6d43af8b-31eb-5d66-898e-79aa49a07672",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Neville Chamberlain, Rothschild family\n- Places: Gunnersbury Park, Sudetenland, Czechoslovakia, Germany\n- Roles: Minister of Health\n- Events: Opening of Gunnersbury Park to the public, Munich Agreement\n- Topics: Appeasement foreign policy\n\nFacts:\n- On 21 May 1926, Neville Chamberlain opened Gunnersbury Park to the public after it was purchased for the nation from the Rothschild family.\n- At the time of the 1926 opening of Gunnersbury Park, Neville Chamberlain was Minister of Health.\n- In 1938, Neville Chamberlain signed the Munich Agreement.\n- The 1938 Munich Agreement conceded the German-speaking Sudetenland region of Czechoslovakia to Germany.\n- Neville Chamberlain is best known for his appeasement foreign policy.",
